6-05-07 DocWorkflow Agent Delivery Testsuite DWT-S4 Summary Telemetry Style Reporting Contract.md:121:- Verification commands name cwd, shell/runtime assumptions, success criteria and blocked commands.\n_specs/2026-05-07 DocWorkflow Agent Delivery Testsuite DWT-S4 Summary Telemetry Style Reporting Contract.md:122:- Evidence and closeout fields distinguish \u0060ran-target\u0060, \u0060ran-rehearsal\u0060, \u0060blocked\u0060, \u0060failed\u0060, \u0060planned\u0060 and \u0060dry-run\u0060.\n_specs/2026-05-07 DocWorkflow Agent Delivery Testsuite DWT-S4 Summary Telemetry Style Reporting Contract.md:132:- Mark runner/auth/network blockers as \u0060blocked\u0060, not \u0060pass\u0060.\n_specs/2026-05-07 DocWorkflow Agent Delivery Testsuite DWT-S4 Summary Telemetry Style Reporting Contract.md:133:- Persist the exact command class and reason for every \u0060warn\u0060, \u0060fail\u0060 or \u0060blocked\u0060 efficiency result.\n_specs/2026-05-07 DocWorkflow Agent Delivery Testsuite DWT-S4 Summary Telemetry Style Reporting Contract.md:137:DWT-S4 may define report fields that DWT-S2 and DWT-S3 later consume. It must not mark those descendants ready. S2/S3 outputs that lack this contract are \u0060planned\u0060 or \u0060blocked\u0060 until their own implementation changes create evidence.\n_specs/2026-05-07 DocWorkflow Agent Delivery Testsuite DWT-S4 Summary Telemetry Style Reporting Contract.md:157:| \u0060tests/docworkflow-agent-delivery/reporting/fixtures/downstream-s2-s3-blocked/\u0060 | Downstream guard fixture. | Missing S2/S3 output contracts remain \u0060blocked\u0060 or \u0060planned\u0060; no descendant release. | Create during DWT-S4 implementation. |\n_specs/2026-05-07 DocWorkflow Agent Delivery Testsuite DWT-S4 Summary Telemetry Style Reporting Contract.md:193:| \u0060DWT-S4-R6\u0060 | Downstream S2/S3 remain blocked until their own contracts exist. | \u0060downstream-s2-s3-blocked\u0060. | \u0060blocked\u0060 or \u0060planned\u0060 for descendants, while DWT-S4